WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.605
Imagine a three-year-old looking up and saying, “I’m ready to get married.

00:00:04.605 --> 00:00:06.882
I would like my own home.

00:00:06.882 --> 00:00:10.776
You may be stunned for a moment, and most of us laugh.

00:00:10.776 --> 00:00:15.842
A real desire can be real before a person is ready to carry its weight.

00:00:15.842 --> 00:00:20.882
Sometimes we ask God to reveal our purpose before we are formed to carry it.

00:00:20.882 --> 00:00:26.868
Moses wanted to free his enslaved brothers, but the desert became a place of formation.

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:31.237
He waited, and God formed him for the mission in God’s timing.

00:00:31.237 --> 00:00:33.605
We are created by God.

00:00:33.605 --> 00:00:42.237
In Christ, our whole life—spirit, mind, body, desires, habits, and work—can be brought back to God.

00:00:42.237 --> 00:00:50.224
Scripture, prayer, a willing attitude, and healthy activity help form us; they are not a spiritual performance.

00:00:50.224 --> 00:00:55.132
Prayer is not dependent on a perfect posture or a perfectly quiet room.

00:00:55.132 --> 00:00:58.566
When you can, turn toward God deliberately.

00:00:58.566 --> 00:01:03.316
What are you asking God to give you, form in you, and help you carry?
